  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_2b1b5069debd45fabb20a9d8dd180d99",
      "statement": "The Fraud class in vn.onepay.pspconnector.provider.onecomm provides the FSP-Go fraud check integration, exposed through static helpers checkFraud(), requestCheckFraud(), isDomesticTransaction(), buildCheckFraudDomesticRequest(), and requestHttp().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Fraud.java#L33-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bca5eb950373f119ccf2408251b7c994b7212d172b2f3522c1fb7b6f48e5003b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c135517af26b44f2b7858cc36b200e6d",
      "statement": "The fraud check is only performed for domestic transactions. checkFraud() selects the fsp-go service and builds a domestic request only when transactionType equals \"domestic\".",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Fraud.java#L43-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d4b254c3398dbf0f6226b2c79e07e6d66e26b0a969b6ccf43f074b5c92e04bb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7a28068b02e54b10b58781f99e409f49",
      "statement": "isDomesticTransaction() classifies a transaction as domestic only when the instrument type is \"card\" or \"np_card\" and the brand ID is \"atm\", both compared case-insensitively.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Fraud.java#L122-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2de6c265e85c74c821c44acb23613f5f965aa1cd11eec61c2e7a3d27f1fa820b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_67f3d38993034d7aa10ad76fd2052440",
      "statement": "The FSP-Go service endpoint is composed from a configured base URL plus the path /domestic/check-fraud, and the HTTP method, authentication credentials (client id, client key, region, service), and timeout are all read from Config system properties.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Config.java#L23-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67fcf23687a2993054ae771c090faba69e537e30de7ccd8023ee3c4cfd2f57bb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Fraud.java#L91-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8e76d7354d7892434486958f627f7f73e00d240aec8dc86ea88eb2d9013cb9a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9636aba57b064b4a849cbc145781c5cb",
      "statement": "Domestic fraud check responses are decided by HTTP status and the \"fraud\" field: a 200 status with a non-empty \"fraud\" field yields Future.failedFuture(TXN_FRAUD); a non-200 status yields Future.failedFuture(INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR); a 200 status with an empty fraud field succeeds the future.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Fraud.java#L67-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d3cb255c9ac99aff168f7a47f70a40cd222bec9e719e035bf8ee51f42ba691a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5c047c35e35046e191fb293d5bd9b95a",
      "statement": "The domestic fraud check request body is built from the purchase request map, extracting payment, instrument, customer, invoice, and payment data sections, and includes a masked card number, card hash, IP address and customer fields read from the raw data (vpc_TicketNo, vpc_Customer_Id, vpc_Customer_Email, vpc_Customer_Phone), with the raw data embedded under the \"data\" key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Fraud.java#L130-L219",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3fa7dc4d4037121b3ed7801f559bb87aad2d3a61d2cbb5ce7fa31d5dfd3d918f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_535b76c578644465aec1c777cbaae3ad",
      "statement": "requestHttp() performs the actual Vert.x HTTP call, signing every request with an Authorization header built from client id, key, region, service, method, path, query parameters, headers, and body, and setting standard headers (X-Op-Date, X-Op-Expires, Content-Type for POST/PUT/PATCH).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Fraud.java#L221-L302",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:84148b806f23a29932fc89d26dedd967403b51d5175dee333cbe2c311efa7186:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_857c80435ce641b6b476217b99551564",
      "statement": "The fraud check is invoked from OnecommPaymentServiceProvider: paymentPurchase() runs it for card/np_card ATM-branded transactions before onecommVerifyCard, and applePayNapasPaymentPurchase() always runs it before applePay; both treat TXN_FRAUD and INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR outcomes as a client-facing 400 \"FRAUD\" error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.java#L297-L333",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8a63956341512d53c0ed4eb0d02c2cbed44de9e4731953932f1593b5e82f615a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.java#L441-L472",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:82070030463aed82cdb205a48782af8c301ba23d82de05d882c7930407386451:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d8071737e7ed4c39b435049db6de2b4a",
      "statement": "All FSP-Go configuration is read from JVM system properties with sensible defaults: URL http://localhost/fsp/api/v2, auth client id PSP-CONNECTOR-ONECOMM, auth service fsp-go, auth region onepay, check fraud method POST, and 60000 ms timeout.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/Config.java#L23-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67fcf23687a2993054ae771c090faba69e537e30de7ccd8023ee3c4cfd2f57bb:"
        }
      ]
    },
